WEBVTT

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.800
I'm afraid it's an irrefutable fact.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:39.780
We only have 89 hours left
before this thing hits the Earth.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.150
Silence, please.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:55.230
W-Well, we've double-checked the data.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.460
Its mass is as great as our planet's...

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.260
We know that!

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.800
That's why we have to intercept it!

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.770
With what? The TODs?

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.840
We could have a hundred, even a thousand,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.540
but an army of ants can't beat an elephant!

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:15.050
Didn't someone say we could
get it if it grew enough in mass?

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.890
Well, not exactly.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.950
We aren't talking about a counterattack,

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:25.530
but there's something called
the Roche Limit in physics.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:32.590
You know that tides are made
by the moon's gravitational pull.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.010
Well, the Earth has a
similar effect on the moon.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:42.380
It causes lunar rocks to be
longer in the Earth's direction.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.580
The reason that the gravity
of the more massive Earth

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:51.080
doesn't completely destroy
the moon is due to distance...

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.720
Please get to the point.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.450
Oh, of course.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:03:00.630
Well, the bottom line is when
two masses get too close,

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:06.230
the tidal effect will destroy the smaller one.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:08.460
So what are you trying to say?

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.700
W-Well, that means...

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:15.310
This alien, when it reaches a certain distance,

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.680
will destroy the Earth
without even making contact.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.650
And that's it.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.570
Wait, we have a plan.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.150
What kind of plan?

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:47.140
The only kind that could
possibly get us out of this.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.810
It's above our heads as we speak.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.830
As low as you can, as fast as you can.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:10.140
Leave it to me.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.960
We're not going to be welcome.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:14.700
That's true.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.940
Don't expect smiles or pats on the back.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.380
But let's go back.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.910
Back to our home.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:36.060
Where are you off to?

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.260
Hey, hey, my sweet Jerusha.

00:04:40.260 --> 00:04:42.470
That's your greeting after all these years?

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.900
No hug, no kiss, just questions?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.140
I guess the answer would be
"a journey of redemption."

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.640
Anyway, gotta go.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.170
Ah, yes...

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:00.680
That "rental car" is for you to use.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:04.990
But you'll have to pay the
bill when you're through.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.480
Wait!

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.190
Why did you turn me into Soma?

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:13.420
Why?

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.920
Intelligence may fuel the embers.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:19.900
But to fill in the gaps, you
need to join the dialogue.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.070
Dr. Noguchi's...

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.870
I was a fan of his, too.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.870
It would be a shame...

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:31.020
...to forget the things he taught us.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:36.870
Wait!

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:38.680
I still have questions!

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:42.650
You're so unrefined...

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.620
It's no fun, right?

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.390
When the mystery is spoiled.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.020
Wait!

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:51.700
So long, people!

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.440
Join the dialogue, huh?

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.670
They must have been good lessons.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:06.640
I didn't think so then.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.010
But I understand now.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:15.590
If that giant alien is also
a disembodied part of Yuri,

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:17.980
I'm sure he can communicate with it...

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.290
That's our last and only hope.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:26.900
Are you watching...

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.060
...Maki?

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:33.070
Up until now, I've been bent on
revenge and killing that thing.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.400
But now...

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.110
We'll be entering the radar
network any second now.

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.460
Low-altitude craft detected.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.930
Aircraft type?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.060
Now inquiring via IFF.

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:07.910
Using a beacon code?

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:26.930
It's an allied cargo flier.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.170
They're having engine trouble

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:32.190
and requesting permission for emergency landing.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:35.100
Hmph, no choice. Guide them in.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:37.810
First runway clear.

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.870
Landing has been approved.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:41.740
Good luck.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.330
Thank you.

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.750
Moving out.

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.740
Wait.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:49.440
I'll go.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.310
You can't.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:55.250
It's my turn.

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.590
Guenevere...

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:59.590
You go to Frank with Hattie.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.970
By the way, that kiss was wonderful.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.760
Casanova.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.890
See you.

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.740
Distance to Funeral Base, 130.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:18.140
SARG 2 will perform a feint
operation to distract the enemy.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.310
Meanwhile, Ryu and Hattie will get on the ground.

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:26.020
The objective is to free Frank from the jail.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.370
Understood.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.110
Yes, sir!

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:34.590
We'll be there soon, Commander.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.370
It can't be.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:53.050
Large cargo ship with heavy
damage landing on runway one.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:55.740
Fire hazard.

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:59.350
All aircraft on standby should
be docked in the hangars.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.140
SARG 2 standing by.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:21.340
Eject!

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.580
Sniping mode!

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:34.980
Fire!

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:59.810
TOD launch bays down.

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.330
Short-wave antenna out.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:02.390
What's going on?

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.470
Errors in Area 24 sensors.
What's going on?

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:07.480
Loading dock entrance inoperable.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:13.960
A SARG...

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.430
And the Mistel.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:18.400
Are they evening the score?

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:28.990
This is insanity!

00:10:28.990 --> 00:10:30.710
The Ulysses?

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:34.040
It's just a huge pile of scrap iron in space!

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:39.250
Now we find out that 30% of
the enormous defense budget

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.420
went to pay for that?

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.290
What was the auditing bureau doing?

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:46.590
Silence, please!

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:52.490
It's true the Ulysses' ability to fire
ballistic missiles at fixed stars

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:55.470
was never a plan that was formally approved.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:11:01.610
But now it could be the one thing
that might solve this crisis.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:03.570
Good point.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:08.310
You should praise our foresight
for including such a feature.

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:11.850
But will it work?

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:15.560
Why don't we ask a professional?

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:18.990
Now connecting with Universal University.

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:23.560
All right, I'll explain as quickly as I can.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:29.070
As you know, a nuclear pulse
engine powers the Ulysses.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:33.040
This involves the detonation of heavy hydrogen

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:37.840
and helium-3 pellets 250 times a second...

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:40.110
Let me just ask you straight out.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:42.740
Can it save us from the current crisis?

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.380
All right.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.610
Well...

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:51.950
Say we detonate all 800 million
nuclear pellets simultaneously.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:55.590
Even allowing for any energy loss,

00:11:55.670 --> 00:12:02.970
we can hit the target with a
blast that's 0.6% of its G-force.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:05.710
The result would cause the target

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:10.240
to miss the Earth by an
estimated 480,000 kilometers.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.960
A high school football team...

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:30.520
...could block better than you guys.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:37.430
Touchdown!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:49.740
Let's go.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.960
Delivery completed.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.120
Roger.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:04.390
Are you all right?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:05.520
I'm fine.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:07.160
Ryu!

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:08.660
It's okay.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:11.160
This is it!

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:17.710
Come on!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:26.120
Call Captain Simmons!

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:27.340
Quickly!

00:13:28.190 --> 00:13:29.920
B-But he's...

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:38.000
What in the hell is happening?

00:13:38.800 --> 00:13:40.440
Come on, let's go.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.740
Where are our intercept aircraft?

00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.140
Relocated to hangars, and
the exit line is damaged.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.950
Repair time, 15 minutes.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.840
Then use the TODs.

00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:00.680
Sorry, all access ways were disabled in the raid.

00:14:05.130 --> 00:14:06.990
TOD fliers, do you read?

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.870
I don't care if you destroy the building!

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.640
Get to the surface using the emergency shafts!

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:13.620
Roger!

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:20.610
Way to go, Lt. Green!

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:23.140
She always gets the job done!

00:14:23.410 --> 00:14:24.880
Don't get careless.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:26.980
We're still warming up.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:28.610
The real bell hasn't rung.

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:39.450
Here come the champions.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.900
Like dark angels from hell.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:50.770
Angels of death.

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.090
Let's do it.

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:20.030
We're fighting those things with this?

00:15:21.800 --> 00:15:23.600
Aren't you the prodigy?

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.710
Easier said than done.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:29.880
But it never hurts to try.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.580
You sure you're ready?

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:38.340
We might not make it out alive.

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:39.510
It's okay.

00:15:39.760 --> 00:15:41.450
Because I'm with you, Ryu.

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:42.880
All right.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:50.910
The problem is the time needed
to turn the Ulysses into a missile.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:52.740
Relax.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.800
All we have to do is send some data commands.

00:15:56.210 --> 00:16:01.230
Well, this is what you all called
a waste of military spending.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:04.440
But we're facing an alien.

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:06.550
Meaning?

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.520
Even if we throw it off course,

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.650
who's to say it won't re-adjust and come back?

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:16.230
We'll deal with the second crisis

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.630
once we get through the first one.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.160
Agreed.

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:22.270
Let's deal with the problem at hand.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.600
Absolutely.

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:30.700
So we're decided.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:33.640
We'll turn the Ulysses into a nuclear missile.

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:35.040
Objection!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.370
The circuit has been hacked from outside.

00:16:39.050 --> 00:16:40.210
Impossible.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.380
That's a military D2 line.

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.390
I object to the decision.

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.920
David Lawrence...

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:53.090
Stop recording.

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:57.100
You're interrupting a council
meeting of the highest order.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.830
Get him off of there.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.060
You should listen first.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.470
Unless you'd rather face a
bigger and more bitter truth.

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:19.350
I have one demand.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:23.760
Postpone the launching of the Ulysses.

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:29.230
This is an extreme situation!

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.500
We can't just stand by while people die!

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:35.470
I'm not saying to let people die.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:37.930
You've got time.

00:17:38.440 --> 00:17:41.040
Your last chance to intercept the target

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.910
will be when it passes the orbit of Mars.

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:46.640
I want you to wait until then.

00:17:53.390 --> 00:17:54.860
At Funeral HQ?

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:57.550
Feeling a little like Henry VI?

00:17:57.630 --> 00:18:02.600
"O, what a scandal is it to our crown."

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:07.240
"Civil dissension is a viperous worm

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:10.430
that gnaws the bowels of the commonwealth."

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:22.380
Damn it, they're having a good time!

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:23.610
Relax, Sue.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:25.180
Are you kidding?

00:18:25.920 --> 00:18:28.150
I'm having an even bigger blast.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:38.370
Attention, please!

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:52.070
Old stunt.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:54.040
I got him!

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.810
Damn you!

00:19:01.720 --> 00:19:03.660
Take that!

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:25.810
You're pretty good.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.510
But this is our home field!

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:32.520
We're not prepared to lose it.

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:41.830
The pipeline!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.240
Like I said.

00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:56.270
This is our home.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.670
Slug mode!

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:11.620
Hmph.

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:13.230
I'm borrowing this.

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:24.410
He's quick!

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.080
Did he turn off his limiter?

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:51.760
A plasma torch?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:01.500
It can't be...

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:12.680
So you're awake now, too...

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.330
Hold on.

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.270
There's a wall over there.

00:21:30.840 --> 00:21:32.000
Let's go that way.

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:33.060
Don't move!

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.380
We've located Ryu Soma

00:21:36.380 --> 00:21:39.810
and someone that looks like
the girl who controls the EX-1.

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.480
On the 11th floor!

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:42.910
Got it.

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:49.060
What is it?

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:50.730
Captain Simmons!

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:53.460
We've caught the rebels.

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.330
I see.

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:02.830
We won't wait for a court-martial.

00:22:04.710 --> 00:22:06.200
How unfortunate.

00:22:12.380 --> 00:22:14.820
That glory that we talked about...

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:16.840
It hasn't become a rusty nail yet.

00:22:18.690 --> 00:22:21.030
Hurry and open your eyes...

00:22:21.920 --> 00:22:22.990
...Yuri.

00:22:36.040 --> 00:22:38.510
When fighting is courage...

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:41.440
When hate comes out of love...

00:22:42.040 --> 00:22:44.910
Then it's time he looks to tomorrow.

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:48.620
Next time,
Courage and Love.
